\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The archival selection, which no limit in this paper escapes. Grey: the spectral-class composition of the Gaia\nobreakspace  {}DR3 objects within 40\,pc that carry a temperature. Blue: the same for the searched sample. Counts are printed above each bar. The sample is enriched in F and G stars by factors of four and three and depleted in M\nobreakspace  {}dwarfs by a factor two, so 21{} of the 5\,908{} classified M\nobreakspace  {}dwarfs within 40\,pc carry a searched window. Because M\nobreakspace  {}dwarfs host most of the habitable-zone planets in the solar neighbourhood, this is the single most important limitation on what the null result means (\S  \ref  {sec:bias}).}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:selbias}{{2}{3}{The archival selection, which no limit in this paper escapes. Grey: the spectral-class composition of the Gaia~DR3 objects within 40\,pc that carry a temperature. Blue: the same for the searched sample. Counts are printed above each bar. The sample is enriched in F and G stars by factors of four and three and depleted in M~dwarfs by a factor two, so \NMSearched {} of the \NMCensus {} classified M~dwarfs within 40\,pc carry a searched window. Because M~dwarfs host most of the habitable-zone planets in the solar neighbourhood, this is the single most important limitation on what the null result means (\S \ref {sec:bias})}{figure.2}{}}
