\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces The visibility-domain test on all 13{} stage-1 windows, one panel each, in units of the measurement uncertainty: the real part of the visibility phase-rotated to the stellar position (blue circle), which emission centred there makes positive and significant; its imaginary part (red square), which such emission leaves consistent with zero; and the real parts returned by eight control positions on the same annulus the image-plane screen uses (open circles). \emph  {Top row:} the 4{} unattributed events, on one shared scale; none reaches $3\sigma $. \emph  {Lower rows:} the 9{} events attributed to carbon monoxide, the test's controls, each panel autoscaled because they reach $59\sigma $.}}{14}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
