\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Two-dimensional sensitivity against window centre frequency for all 1655{} searched windows, symbol by channelisation class, the axis along which completeness differs (Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:classcomp}). \emph  {Left axis}: the nominal trigger threshold $P_{\rm  trig}$, an internal detection statistic. \emph  {Right axis}: the effective threshold at the \emph  {median} response, $P_{\rm  eff}=2.29\,P_{\rm  trig}$, which is the power to compare with a transmitter (\S  \ref  {sec:method}); the per-window ratio $P_{\rm  eff,total}/P_{\rm  trig}$ runs $1.33$--$3.98$, so a single window's threshold should be read from the catalogue, not from this axis. Red rings mark the 9{} windows whose smearing correction exceeds 1 per cent; dotted, the Arecibo 2.38-GHz benchmark. Note the two decades of scatter at fixed frequency: there is no single survey sensitivity.}}{17}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
