\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces The prospective epoch extension against the frozen science sample. Every frozen-column number is computed from the released catalogue by the same definition applied to the extension, and the generator cross-asserts them against the macros the rest of the paper uses, so the two columns are like for like. The extension is \emph  {not} pooled into the sample: it was searched after the statistic and the mask were fixed. The last three lines carry the result --- the attributed events are all the $\beta $\nobreakspace  {}Pictoris disc, the unattributed count is zero, and the add-one rank is displaced from 0.5 by about as much as in the sample itself, on windows the statistic had never seen.}}{24}{table.10}\protected@file@percent }
