\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Per-band survey characterisation of the 1655 searched windows. ``Sys.'' counts unique stellar systems searched in the band, so a system observed in two bands is counted in both rows (82 systems, 90 stars in total); ``EBs'' the contributing execution blocks, attributed by the provenance of the de-duplicated windows; $\Delta \nu _{\rm  ch}$ the native channel width in MHz (median, range in brackets); ``Union'' the unique sky frequency searched in the band after merging overlapping windows; EIRP$_{5\sigma }$ the median nominal threshold across the band's windows; $\dot  {\nu }_{\rm  ceil}$ the range of drift-rate ceilings in Hz\,s$^{-1}$ per GHz of carrier frequency. The ``All'' row is computed over the whole sample, not summed down the columns: EBs and systems recur across bands and the frequency unions are disjoint by construction.}}{31}{table.14}\protected@file@percent }
